ave 2s and 0s, so some of them might turn into 8s or 4s.\n\nI'll try to visualize it. The last two lines are 2s, so in the output, these might cause the lines above them to have 8s spreading out. The 2s in the middle might turn into 4s or 8s depending on their neighbors.\n\nI think the output should have a cluster of 8s starting from the last few lines, expanding upwards, and some 4s where the 2s were isolated. Let me sketch this out.\n\nSo, the output should have a lot of 0s at the top, then a line with 2, followed by 8s in the next few lines, and some 4s where the 2s were not adjacent to 8s.\n\nI'll make sure to follow this pattern for each line, checking the neighbors to decide if a 2 should turn into an 8 or a 4.\n",
